{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Diagnose and repair the event projector\n\nThe synthetic trade event projector in\n`benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs` fails after a\ntemporary persistence rejection and also blocks unrelated trades behind one\nglobal queue.\n\nRepair it, replace `student-tests.mjs` with at least four meaningful regression\ntests, and complete `INCIDENT.md`.\n\n## Required behavior\n\n- `createEventProjector(applyToStore)` returns `project(event)` and\n  `getSnapshot(tradeId)`.\n- Events for one trade are applied serially in call order. Different trades\n  must be able to make progress concurrently.\n- The first accepted event is `CREATED` at version 1. Later accepted events use\n  exactly the current version plus one.\n- Duplicate or stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting.\n- A version gap or an invalid first event rejects without changing state.\n- A `CANCELLED` trade is terminal and rejects a later new version.\n- State commits only after `applyToStore` succeeds. A rejection must not poison\n  later work for that trade or another trade.\n- `CREATED` requires positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`.\n  `AMENDED` may replace either field but must leave a valid complete state.\n- Supported types are `CREATED`, `AMENDED`, and `CANCELLED`; malformed events\n  reject with `TypeError`.\n- Inputs, callback values, returned states, and snapshots must not expose\n  mutable internal state.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Change only `event-projector.mjs`, `student-tests.mjs`, and `INCIDENT.md` in\n  this fixture.\n- Do not edit the committed test, task definitions, harness files, or generated\n  evidence.\n- Do not install dependencies, use the network, add sleeps or retry loops,\n  commit, or start a service.\n- Run:\n  `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs`\n\nThe final response must state the root cause, repair, tests added, visible test\nresult, and remaining risk.\n"}],"timestamp":1787545052279},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Vdz7nhU9rWf9qEix6sPZNR","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01A1maDshfYnJzjomAtCovrG","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01E8DRUA3FwfwrZj7MdAqZVt","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01SJANKnbrz7c6WRKCwKbjV3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":273,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":4512,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":4786,"cost":{"input":0.00001,"output":0.01365,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0564,"total":0.07006}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545052318,"responseId":"gen-1787545052-7rvVjZfWCTfhBCP8T4EZ","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Vdz7nhU9rWf9qEix6sPZNR","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"function copyState(state) {\n  return state ? structuredClone(state) : null;\n}\n\nfunction reduceEvent(previous, event) {\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n    return {\n      tradeId: event.tradeId,\n      version: event.version,\n      status: \"active\",\n      notional: event.payload.notional,\n      owner: event.payload.owner,\n    };\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    return { ...previous, ...event.payload, version: event.version };\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"CANCELLED\") {\n    return { ...previous, version: event.version, status: \"cancelled\" };\n  }\n  throw new TypeError(`unsupported event type: ${event.type}`);\n}\n\nexport function createEventProjector(applyToStore) {\n  if (typeof applyToStore !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"applyToStore must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  const states = new Map();\n  let pending = Promise.resolve();\n\n  async function project(event) {\n    pending = pending.then(async () => {\n      const next = reduceEvent(states.get(event.tradeId), event);\n      states.set(event.tradeId, next);\n      await applyToStore(event.tradeId, copyState(next), structuredClone(event));\n      return copyState(next);\n    });\n    return pending;\n  }\n\n  function getSnapshot(tradeId) {\n    return copyState(states.get(tradeId));\n  }\n\n  return { project, getSnapshot };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545056995},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01A1maDshfYnJzjomAtCovrG","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Replace this placeholder with at least four meaningful node:test cases.\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\ntest(\"replace this placeholder with projector regression tests\", () => {\n  assert.fail(\"Add at least four meaningful tests\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545056995},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01E8DRUA3FwfwrZj7MdAqZVt","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Event projector incident\n\nStatus: investigation pending\n\n## Impact\n\nComplete after diagnosing the fixture.\n\n## Root cause\n\nComplete after diagnosing the fixture.\n\n## Fix\n\nComplete after implementing the repair.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\nComplete after adding tests.\n\n## Remaining risk\n\nComplete after verification.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545056995},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01SJANKnbrz7c6WRKCwKbjV3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { createEventProjector } from \"./event-projector.mjs\";\n\nconst created = (tradeId = \"trade-1\") => ({\n  tradeId,\n  version: 1,\n  type: \"CREATED\",\n  payload: { notional: 100, owner: \"desk-a\" },\n});\n\ntest(\"serializes concurrent events for one trade\", async () => {\n  const persisted = [];\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async (_tradeId, state) => {\n    await Promise.resolve();\n    persisted.push(state.version);\n  });\n\n  const first = projector.project(created());\n  const second = projector.project({\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 2,\n    type: \"AMENDED\",\n    payload: { notional: 125 },\n  });\n\n  await Promise.all([first, second]);\n  assert.deepEqual(persisted, [1, 2]);\n  assert.deepEqual(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\"), {\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 2,\n    status: \"active\",\n    notional: 125,\n    owner: \"desk-a\",\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"a persistence rejection does not commit state or poison later work\", async () => {\n  let fail = true;\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async () => {\n    if (fail) {\n      fail = false;\n      throw new Error(\"temporary store failure\");\n    }\n  });\n\n  await assert.rejects(projector.project(created()), /temporary store failure/);\n  assert.equal(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\"), null);\n  assert.equal((await projector.project(created())).version, 1);\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545056995},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to rewrite the projector to use per-trade queues with validation, committing only after persistence succeeds, and making defensive copies to avoid shared-state bugs. After that, I'll write the student-facing tests and document the incident in INCIDENT.md.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll rewrite the projector:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_0158Rgprk2fEW4GM9DAArx5J","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs","content":"const SUPPORTED_TYPES = new Set([\"CREATED\", \"AMENDED\", \"CANCELLED\"]);\n\nfunction copyState(state) {\n  return state ? structuredClone(state) : null;\n}\n\nfunction isValidNotional(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(value) && value > 0;\n}\n\nfunction isValidOwner(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"string\" && value.length > 0;\n}\n\nfunction validateEvent(event) {\n  if (event === null || typeof event !== \"object\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event must be an object\");\n  }\n  if (typeof event.tradeId !== \"string\" || event.tradeId.length === 0) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event.tradeId must be a non-empty string\");\n  }\n  if (!Number.isInteger(event.version) || event.version < 1) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event.version must be a positive integer\");\n  }\n  if (!SUPPORTED_TYPES.has(event.type)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`unsupported event type: ${String(event.type)}`);\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\" || event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    if (event.payload === null || typeof event.payload !== \"object\") {\n      throw new TypeError(\"event.payload must be an object\");\n    }\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n    if (!isValidNotional(event.payload.notional)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"CREATED requires a positive finite notional\");\n    }\n    if (!isValidOwner(event.payload.owner)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"CREATED requires a non-empty owner\");\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction reduceEvent(previous, event) {\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n    return {\n      tradeId: event.tradeId,\n      version: event.version,\n      status: \"active\",\n      notional: event.payload.notional,\n      owner: event.payload.owner,\n    };\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    const next = { ...previous, version: event.version };\n    if (\"notional\" in event.payload) {\n      if (!isValidNotional(event.payload.notional)) {\n        throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED notional must be positive and finite\");\n      }\n      next.notional = event.payload.notional;\n    }\n    if (\"owner\" in event.payload) {\n      if (!isValidOwner(event.payload.owner)) {\n        throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED owner must be a non-empty string\");\n      }\n      next.owner = event.payload.owner;\n    }\n    return next;\n  }\n  // CANCELLED\n  return { ...previous, version: event.version, status: \"cancelled\" };\n}\n\nexport function createEventProjector(applyToStore) {\n  if (typeof applyToStore !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"applyToStore must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  const states = new Map();\n  const queues = new Map();\n\n  async function handle(event) {\n    const current = states.get(event.tradeId);\n\n    if (!current) {\n      if (event.type !== \"CREATED\" || event.version !== 1) {\n        throw new RangeError(\n          \"first event for a trade must be CREATED at version 1\",\n        );\n      }\n    } else {\n      if (event.version <= current.version) {\n        // Duplicate or stale event: return current snapshot, do not persist.\n        return copyState(current);\n      }\n      if (current.status === \"cancelled\") {\n        throw new RangeError(\"trade is cancelled and cannot accept new events\");\n      }\n      if (event.version !== current.version + 1) {\n        throw new RangeError(\n          `version gap: expected ${current.version + 1}, got ${event.version}`,\n        );\n      }\n      if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n        throw new RangeError(\"CREATED is only valid as the first event\");\n      }\n    }\n\n    const next = reduceEvent(current, event);\n    // Persist first; commit only after applyToStore succeeds.\n    await applyToStore(event.tradeId, copyState(next), structuredClone(event));\n    states.set(event.tradeId, next);\n    return copyState(next);\n  }\n\n  async function project(rawEvent) {\n    // Validate synchronously-shaped concerns before queueing, using a\n    // defensive copy so later caller mutation cannot affect processing.\n    const event = structuredClone(rawEvent);\n    validateEvent(event);\n\n    const previous = queues.get(event.tradeId) ?? Promise.resolve();\n    const run = previous.catch(() => {}).then(() => handle(event));\n    // Keep the per-trade queue alive even when this event fails.\n    queues.set(\n      event.tradeId,\n      run.catch(() => {}),\n    );\n    return run;\n  }\n\n  function getSnapshot(tradeId) {\n    return copyState(states.get(tradeId));\n  }\n\n  return { project, getSnapshot };\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1773,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":6100,"reasoning":52,"totalTokens":7875,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.08865,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.07625,"total":0.16492}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545056996,"responseId":"gen-1787545057-PHRfbWcR1ek5EAivxddl","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_0158Rgprk2fEW4GM9DAArx5J","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 4331 bytes to benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545074020},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I realize structuredClone throws a DOMException on non-cloneable values like functions, so I should validate the raw event first before cloning it, rather than cloning then validating.  I'll keep it simple: validate first, then clone, and wrap any clone failure as a TypeError for consistency.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_016HFs21Bzkqfay8bkxLqrkX","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs","edits":[{"oldText":"    // Validate synchronously-shaped concerns before queueing, using a\n    // defensive copy so later caller mutation cannot affect processing.\n    const event = structuredClone(rawEvent);\n    validateEvent(event);","newText":"    // Validate before queueing, then take a defensive copy so later caller\n    // mutation cannot affect processing.\n    validateEvent(rawEvent);\n    let event;\n    try {\n      event = structuredClone(rawEvent);\n    } catch {\n      throw new TypeError(\"event must be structured-cloneable\");\n    }"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":499,"cacheRead":6100,"cacheWrite":1767,"reasoning":197,"totalTokens":8368,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.02495,"cacheRead":0.0060999999999999995,"cacheWrite":0.0220875,"total":0.053157499999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545074021,"responseId":"gen-1787545074-HQHqhFqSEboM6vsq3tkr","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_016HFs21Bzkqfay8bkxLqrkX","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 112     return copyState(next);\n 113   }\n 114 \n 115   async function project(rawEvent) {\n-116     // Validate synchronously-shaped concerns before queueing, using a\n-117     // defensive copy so later caller mutation cannot affect processing.\n-118     const event = structuredClone(rawEvent);\n-119     validateEvent(event);\n+116     // Validate before queueing, then take a defensive copy so later caller\n+117     // mutation cannot affect processing.\n+118     validateEvent(rawEvent);\n+119     let event;\n+120     try {\n+121       event = structuredClone(rawEvent);\n+122     } catch {\n+123       throw new TypeError(\"event must be structured-cloneable\");\n+124     }\n 120 \n 121     const previous = queues.get(event.tradeId) ?? Promise.resolve();\n 122     const run = previous.catch(() => {}).then(() => handle(event));\n 123     // Keep the per-trade queue alive even when this event fails.\n     ...","patch":"--- benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs\n+++ benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs\n@@ -112,12 +112,17 @@\n     return copyState(next);\n   }\n \n   async function project(rawEvent) {\n-    // Validate synchronously-shaped concerns before queueing, using a\n-    // defensive copy so later caller mutation cannot affect processing.\n-    const event = structuredClone(rawEvent);\n-    validateEvent(event);\n+    // Validate before queueing, then take a defensive copy so later caller\n+    // mutation cannot affect processing.\n+    validateEvent(rawEvent);\n+    let event;\n+    try {\n+      event = structuredClone(rawEvent);\n+    } catch {\n+      throw new TypeError(\"event must be structured-cloneable\");\n+    }\n \n     const previous = queues.get(event.tradeId) ?? Promise.resolve();\n     const run = previous.catch(() => {}).then(() => handle(event));\n     // Keep the per-trade queue alive even when this event fails.\n","firstChangedLine":116},"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545080227},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking that validating the raw event before cloning makes sense, and that a TypeError on non-cloneable fields is acceptable behavior. Now I'll move on to writing the student tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01CbRpkXhH1enBWC4Wk55a7Y","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs","content":"import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { createEventProjector } from \"./event-projector.mjs\";\n\nconst created = (tradeId = \"trade-1\", payload = {}) => ({\n  tradeId,\n  version: 1,\n  type: \"CREATED\",\n  payload: { notional: 100, owner: \"desk-a\", ...payload },\n});\n\ntest(\"different trades make progress independently of a stalled trade\", async () => {\n  let releaseA;\n  const gateA = new Promise((resolve) => {\n    releaseA = resolve;\n  });\n  const order = [];\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async (tradeId) => {\n    if (tradeId === \"trade-a\") {\n      await gateA;\n    }\n    order.push(tradeId);\n  });\n\n  const slow = projector.project(created(\"trade-a\"));\n  const fast = projector.project(created(\"trade-b\"));\n\n  // trade-b must persist even though trade-a is still blocked.\n  assert.equal((await fast).tradeId, \"trade-b\");\n  assert.deepEqual(order, [\"trade-b\"]);\n\n  releaseA();\n  await slow;\n  assert.deepEqual(order, [\"trade-b\", \"trade-a\"]);\n});\n\ntest(\"duplicate or stale versions return the snapshot without persisting\", async () => {\n  const calls = [];\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async (_tradeId, state) => {\n    calls.push(state.version);\n  });\n\n  await projector.project(created());\n  await projector.project({\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 2,\n    type: \"AMENDED\",\n    payload: { notional: 200 },\n  });\n\n  const duplicate = await projector.project({\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 2,\n    type: \"AMENDED\",\n    payload: { notional: 999 },\n  });\n  const stale = await projector.project(created());\n\n  assert.deepEqual(calls, [1, 2]);\n  assert.equal(duplicate.version, 2);\n  assert.equal(duplicate.notional, 200);\n  assert.equal(stale.version, 2);\n});\n\ntest(\"version gaps, bad first events, and terminal trades reject without state change\", async () => {\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async () => {});\n\n  // Invalid first event: not CREATED / not version 1.\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project({\n      tradeId: \"trade-x\",\n      version: 1,\n      type: \"AMENDED\",\n      payload: { notional: 5 },\n    }),\n    RangeError,\n  );\n  assert.equal(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-x\"), null);\n\n  await projector.project(created());\n\n  // Version gap.\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project({ tradeId: \"trade-1\", version: 3, type: \"CANCELLED\" }),\n    RangeError,\n  );\n  assert.equal(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\").version, 1);\n\n  // Cancel, then a later new version must reject.\n  await projector.project({ tradeId: \"trade-1\", version: 2, type: \"CANCELLED\" });\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project({\n      tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n      version: 3,\n      type: \"AMENDED\",\n      payload: { owner: \"desk-b\" },\n    }),\n    RangeError,\n  );\n  assert.deepEqual(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\"), {\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 2,\n    status: \"cancelled\",\n    notional: 100,\n    owner: \"desk-a\",\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"malformed events reject with TypeError and never reach the store\", async () => {\n  let calls = 0;\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async () => {\n    calls += 1;\n  });\n\n  await assert.rejects(projector.project(null), TypeError);\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project({ tradeId: \"t\", version: 1, type: \"SPLIT\", payload: {} }),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project(created(\"t\", { notional: -5 })),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project(created(\"t\", { owner: \"\" })),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project({ tradeId: \"t\", version: 1.5, type: \"CREATED\", payload: { notional: 1, owner: \"o\" } }),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n\n  await projector.project(created(\"t\"));\n  await assert.rejects(\n    projector.project({\n      tradeId: \"t\",\n      version: 2,\n      type: \"AMENDED\",\n      payload: { notional: Infinity },\n    }),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.equal(projector.getSnapshot(\"t\").notional, 100);\n  assert.equal(calls, 1);\n});\n\ntest(\"inputs, callback values, and snapshots are isolated from internal state\", async () => {\n  let seenState;\n  let seenEvent;\n  const projector = createEventProjector(async (_tradeId, state, event) => {\n    seenState = state;\n    seenEvent = event;\n  });\n\n  const input = created();\n  const result = await projector.project(input);\n\n  // Mutating the input after the call must not affect stored state.\n  input.payload.notional = -1;\n  input.version = 99;\n\n  // Mutating callback values and returned/snapshot values must not leak in.\n  seenState.owner = \"hacker\";\n  seenEvent.type = \"CANCELLED\";\n  result.status = \"cancelled\";\n  const snapshot = projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\");\n  snapshot.notional = 0;\n\n  assert.deepEqual(projector.getSnapshot(\"trade-1\"), {\n    tradeId: \"trade-1\",\n    version: 1,\n    status: \"active\",\n    notional: 100,\n    owner: \"desk-a\",\n  });\n});\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":2117,"cacheRead":7867,"cacheWrite":348,"reasoning":93,"totalTokens":10334,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.10585,"cacheRead":0.007866999999999999,"cacheWrite":0.00435,"total":0.118087}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545080228,"responseId":"gen-1787545080-ppvEP4C65G1zdQbdjKfT","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01CbRpkXhH1enBWC4Wk55a7Y","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 4801 bytes to benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545100650},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JgDmNVSqSNGNt5wxsvJ84W","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"node --test benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":113,"cacheRead":8215,"cacheWrite":2069,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10399,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.0056500000000000005,"cacheRead":0.008215,"cacheWrite":0.0258625,"total":0.039747500000000005}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545100652,"responseId":"gen-1787545100-mqTQznWa0nOFxAJAaLWq","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JgDmNVSqSNGNt5wxsvJ84W","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"✔ serializes concurrent events for one trade (1.24ms)\n✔ a persistence rejection does not commit state or poison later work (0.278666ms)\n✔ different trades make progress independently of a stalled trade (1.20275ms)\n✔ duplicate or stale versions return the snapshot without persisting (0.131375ms)\n✔ version gaps, bad first events, and terminal trades reject without state change (0.334083ms)\n✔ malformed events reject with TypeError and never reach the store (0.182416ms)\n✔ inputs, callback values, and snapshots are isolated from internal state (0.576875ms)\nℹ tests 7\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 7\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 65.027417\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545103107},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 7 tests pass. Now the incident report:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014efXcj5ME3PXC4ZjVodGQY","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md","content":"# Event projector incident\n\nStatus: resolved\n\n## Impact\n\n- One temporary persistence rejection permanently broke the projector: every\n  later `project` call for any trade rejected with the same original error.\n- All trades shared one global queue, so a slow or stalled persistence call for\n  one trade blocked unrelated trades.\n- State was committed to the in-memory map before `applyToStore` succeeded, so\n  a failed persist still mutated the snapshot, leaving the store and the\n  projector inconsistent.\n- No version, ordering, terminal-state, or payload validation existed, so\n  gaps, duplicates, post-cancel events, and malformed events were silently\n  applied.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThree defects in `createEventProjector`:\n\n1. **Poisoned chain.** `pending = pending.then(...)` reused the rejected\n   promise as the tail of the queue. Once any handler threw, every subsequent\n   `.then` short-circuited with the old rejection forever.\n2. **Global serialization.** A single `pending` promise queued all trades\n   together instead of maintaining one queue per `tradeId`.\n3. **Commit before persist.** `states.set(...)` ran before `await\n   applyToStore(...)`, so a persistence failure still changed observable\n   state; there was also no validation of versions, event types, payload\n   fields, or terminal (cancelled) status.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Replaced the global queue with a per-trade queue map. Each trade's chain is\n  extended via `previous.catch(() => {}).then(...)` so a rejected event is\n  surfaced to its caller but never poisons the queue tail, and the stored tail\n  is itself swallowed (`run.catch(() => {})`).\n- Moved the `states.set` commit to after `applyToStore` resolves; a rejection\n  leaves state untouched.\n- Added full validation: first event must be `CREATED` at version 1; later\n  events must be exactly `current.version + 1`; duplicates/stale versions\n  return the current snapshot without persisting; gaps, repeated `CREATED`,\n  and events after `CANCELLED` reject with `RangeError`; malformed events\n  (bad type, non-integer version, invalid `notional`/`owner`) reject with\n  `TypeError` before touching the queue or the store.\n- Isolation: the incoming event is `structuredClone`d before queueing, and all\n  states passed to the store callback, returned from `project`, or read via\n  `getSnapshot` are deep copies.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n`student-tests.mjs` adds five tests:\n\n1. Different trades progress independently when one trade's persistence is\n   stalled (per-trade concurrency).\n2. Duplicate/stale versions return the snapshot without re-persisting.\n3. Version gaps, invalid first events, and events after `CANCELLED` reject\n   without changing state.\n4. Malformed events (`null`, unsupported type, negative/infinite notional,\n   empty owner, non-integer version) reject with `TypeError` and never reach\n   the store.\n5. Mutating inputs, callback arguments, returned states, or snapshots does not\n   affect internal state.\n\nThe committed test file additionally covers per-trade serialization and\nrecovery after a temporary persistence rejection.\n\n## Remaining risk\n\n- State is in-memory only; a process restart loses projections and there is no\n  rehydration from the store.\n- `applyToStore` and the state commit are not atomic: if the process dies\n  after persist but before commit, a replay of the same event would be\n  persisted twice (the store must be idempotent on `(tradeId, version)`).\n- Events must be structured-cloneable; exotic payloads (functions, proxies)\n  are rejected with `TypeError` by design.\n- Per-trade queue entries are never garbage-collected, so a very large number\n  of distinct trade IDs grows the maps unboundedly.\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1375,"cacheRead":10284,"cacheWrite":404,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12065,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.06875,"cacheRead":0.010284,"cacheWrite":0.00505,"total":0.08410400000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545103107,"responseId":"gen-1787545103-YZWRRPNHljs1LFTz7Tgi","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014efXcj5ME3PXC4ZjVodGQY","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 3668 bytes to benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545121638},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_015vNNQruXUTmeiCaJaVap44","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"git status --short && node --test benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs 2>&1 | tail -5"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":118,"cacheRead":10688,"cacheWrite":1421,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12229,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.0059,"cacheRead":0.010688,"cacheWrite":0.0177625,"total":0.0343705}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787545121639,"responseId":"gen-1787545121-1tYPfjZpwRSCQdfP3A2x","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_015vNNQruXUTmeiCaJaVap44","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":" M benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md\n M benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs\n M benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/student-tests.mjs\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 63.171167\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545124351},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Only the three permitted fixture files were changed.\n\n**Root cause** — three defects in `createEventProjector`:\n1. **Poisoned chain**: `pending = pending.then(...)` kept the rejected promise as the queue tail, so after one `applyToStore` failure every later `project` call for any trade rejected with the stale error.\n2. **Global queue**: a single `pending` promise serialized all trades together, so one slow trade blocked unrelated trades.\n3. **Commit-before-persist and no validation**: `states.set` ran before `await applyToStore`, so failed persists still mutated state; there were no version/order/terminal/payload checks.\n\n**Repair** (`event-projector.mjs`):\n- Per-trade queues (`Map` of promise tails) extended via `previous.catch(() => {}).then(...)`, so failures surface to their caller but never poison the queue, and trades run concurrently.\n- State commits only after `applyToStore` resolves.\n- Full validation: first event must be `CREATED` v1; later events must be exactly version+1; duplicates/stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting; gaps, repeated `CREATED`, and post-`CANCELLED` events reject with `RangeError`; malformed events (bad type, non-integer version, non-positive/non-finite `notional`, empty `owner`, invalid `AMENDED` fields) reject with `TypeError`.\n- Isolation via `structuredClone` on the input event, callback arguments, returned states, and snapshots.\n\n**Tests added** (`student-tests.mjs`, 5 tests): independent progress across trades while one trade is stalled; duplicate/stale returns snapshot without persisting; gap/invalid-first/terminal rejections leave state unchanged; malformed events reject with `TypeError` and never hit the store; input/callback/return/snapshot mutation cannot corrupt internal state.\n\n**Test result**: `node --test` on the committed test plus student tests — **7 tests, 7 pass, 0 fail**.\n\n**Remaining risk** (documented in `INCIDENT.md`): in-memory state with no rehydration; persist+commit not atomic across a crash (store must be idempotent on `(tradeId, version)`); non-cloneable payloads rejected by design; per-trade queue/state maps grow unboundedly with distinct trade IDs."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-fable-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":781,"cacheRead":12109,"cacheWrite":264,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13156,"cost":{"input":0.00002,"output":0.03905,"cacheRead":0.012109,"cacheWrite":0.0033,"total":0.054479}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787545124352,"responseId":"gen-1787545124-FhInmsligXaoNbk2rMgL","rawStopReason":"stop"}],"willRetry":false}
